.nh
.TH "TEAMS" "1" "Oct 2026" "teams dev" "teams Manual"

.SH NAME
teams-mentions - Show the messages that mention you


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBteams mentions [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Show the messages that mention you, newest first. The search runs with
IsMentioned:true and a sent>= window, and the timestamps are checked again on
the client, which is what makes --since exact (PLAN.md:233). The default
window is 24h.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for mentions

.PP
\fB--limit\fP=25
	results per page (the API allows up to 50)

.PP
\fB--since\fP=""
	only mentions newer than this (default 24h; a duration or a timestamp)

.PP
\fB--until\fP=""
	only mentions older than this (a duration or a timestamp)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--jq\fP=""
	filter JSON output through a jq expression (implies --json)

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	machine-readable JSON output

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	disable colours (also honours NO_COLOR)

.PP
\fB--no-input\fP[=false]
	never prompt; fail fast instead

.PP
\fB--profile\fP=""
	profile to use (default: the configured default_profile)

.PP
\fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	suppress progress messages on stderr

.PP
\fB--read-only\fP[=false]
	refuse write commands

.PP
\fB--refresh\fP[=false]
	ignore cached names and resolve them again

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=0]
	verbose diagnostics on stderr (-v, -vv)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBteams(1)\fP
